From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: marty <marty@fyai.co.nz>
Date: Sun, 7 Sep 2026 23:00:00 +1200
Subject: [PATCH] Subtitles: put the size in the in-player dialog

The subtitle dialog reachable while a video plays offers enable, delay, stream,
browse and search - everything except the one thing you look at the subtitles
and want to change. Size lives in Kodi's settings tree at level Advanced, so on
a box left at the default Standard level it is never drawn at all, and reaching
it means raising a global settings level and leaving whatever you are watching.

Adding it here puts it on the one screen that is open while the subtitles are
in front of you to be judged against. CSubtitlesSettings already registers a
callback on subtitles.fontsize and notifies its observers, so the change lands
immediately instead of on the next video.

The range is Kodi's own: 12 to 74 in steps of 2.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/xbmc/video/dialogs/GUIDialogSubtitleSettings.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/video/dialogs/GUIDialogSubtitleSettings.cpp
@@ -50,6 +50,9 @@
 #define SETTING_SUBTITLE_STREAM                "subtitles.stream"
 #define SETTING_SUBTITLE_BROWSER               "subtitles.browser"
 #define SETTING_SUBTITLE_SEARCH                "subtitles.search"
+// Distinct from CSettings::SETTING_SUBTITLES_FONTSIZE: this dialog keeps its
+// settings in its own manager, and reusing the id there invites confusion.
+#define SETTING_SUBTITLE_FONTSIZE             "subtitles.osdfontsize"
 #define SETTING_MAKE_DEFAULT                   "audio.makedefault"
 
 CGUIDialogSubtitleSettings::CGUIDialogSubtitleSettings()
@@ -117,6 +120,12 @@
     m_subtitleStream = std::static_pointer_cast<const CSettingInt>(setting)->GetValue();
     appPlayer->SetSubtitle(m_subtitleStream);
   }
+  else if (settingId == SETTING_SUBTITLE_FONTSIZE)
+  {
+    const int value = std::static_pointer_cast<const CSettingInt>(setting)->GetValue();
+    CServiceBroker::GetSettingsComponent()->GetSettings()->SetInt(
+        CSettings::SETTING_SUBTITLES_FONTSIZE, value);
+  }
 }
 
 std::string CGUIDialogSubtitleSettings::BrowseForSubtitle()
@@ -318,6 +327,19 @@
     std::static_pointer_cast<CSettingControlSlider>(settingSubtitleDelay->GetControl())->SetFormatter(SettingFormatterDelay);
   }
 
+  // subtitle size setting
+  //
+  // The only place a viewer can reach this. Kodi keeps subtitles.fontsize at
+  // settings level Advanced, so on a box left at the default Standard level it
+  // is not merely buried, it is never drawn - and it was absent from here, the
+  // one screen open while the subtitles are on screen to be judged against.
+  // CSubtitlesSettings watches the setting and notifies its observers, so the
+  // change shows immediately rather than on the next video.
+  AddSpinner(groupSubtitles, SETTING_SUBTITLE_FONTSIZE, 289, SettingLevel::Basic,
+             CServiceBroker::GetSettingsComponent()->GetSettings()->GetInt(
+                 CSettings::SETTING_SUBTITLES_FONTSIZE),
+             12, 2, 74);
+
   // subtitle stream setting
   if (SupportsSubtitleFeature(IPlayerSubtitleCaps::SELECT_STREAM))
     AddSubtitleStreams(groupSubtitles, SETTING_SUBTITLE_STREAM);
